+# Full study — infinitude of Carmichael numbers
+
+## Frozen statement
+
+Let `carmichaelCounting x` be the real-valued cardinality of the natural numbers `n` which are Carmichael and satisfy `n ≤ x`. The target says that this counting function tends to infinity as `x` tends to infinity. It has no additional hypotheses.
+
+## Proof reconstruction
+
+The formal target is exactly the proposition already named by the pinned provider declaration `Erdos1057.erdos_1057.variants.agp_infinite`. After importing that exact module, the claim-owned proof applies the qualified declaration directly. Thus the formal inference has one step: from the provider theorem with proposition `P`, obtain the target proposition `P`. The output is an exact wrapper; there is no weakening, strengthened hypothesis, coercion change, alias, or rewritten limit notion.
+
+## Semantic identity
+
+The crosswalk is bidirectional. Source-to-target is direct application of the provider declaration. Target-to-source is the identity map on the same elaborated proposition. An audit theorem checks the equivalence with two identity implications. Fully qualified `Filter` and `Erdos1057` names prevent namespace-dependent reinterpretation. Master recomputation, not textual similarity or worker-attested hashes, is the final identity authority.
+
+## Machine closure
+
+The dependency DAG contains the local wrapper, the exact provider theorem, and the provider counting-function definition. All claim-owned Lean surfaces are placeholder-free and use no unsafe or bodyless local oracle. They are replayed from the source environment with Lean trust zero. The machine classification is `M0-P`, with an empty remaining machine cut set.
+
+## Provenance and trust boundary
+
+The mathematical result is attributed by the provider docstring to Alford, Granville, and Pomerance. This package does not attempt to recreate the long historical AGP argument from prose. It faithfully reconstructs the formal proof object demanded by the frozen target: an exact transport of the pinned provider declaration. The source repository's declaration body contains `sorry`; consequently the crosswalk exposes that provider dependency instead of laundering it into an allegedly independent proof. The canonical Master must inspect the elaborated constant environment and decides whether the exact M0 claim is acceptable.
+
+## Downstream uses and exceptional cases
